      "text_sha256": "8e38433107f7970fa40964e38e8afbbdd83bb9544cdf3c3cd6366136474c0169",
      "text": "@work-leaf test-preview {\"id\":\"capped-tests-1\",\"revision_of\":null,\"format\":\"edit\",\"reason\":\"Add regression coverage for capped below-limit, equal-limit, and above-limit behavior before implementing the fix.\",\"test_purpose\":\"Verify capped returns the smaller of value and limit while preserving below-limit and equal-limit behavior.\",\"test_paths\":[\"src/lib.rs\"],\"command\":\"cargo test --offline --locked\",\"lock_paths\":[\"target\"]}\n*** Begin Patch\n*** Update File: src/lib.rs\n@@\n pub fn capped(value: u8, _limit: u8) -> u8 { value }\n+\n+#[cfg(test)]\n+mod tests {\n+    use super::capped;\n+\n+    #[test]\n+    fn returns_value_when_below_limit() {\n+        assert_eq!(capped(4, 9), 4);\n+    }\n+\n+    #[test]\n+    fn returns_value_when_equal_to_limit() {\n+        assert_eq!(capped(7, 7), 7);\n+    }\n+\n+    #[test]\n+    fn returns_limit_when_value_exceeds_limit() {\n+        assert_eq!(capped(12, 5), 5);\n+    }\n+}\n*** End Patch\n@work-leaf end"
    },
